    "body": "So instead of\r\n\r\n> It therefore only superficially matches the GB18030-2022 standard for code points encoded as four bytes.\r\n\r\nmaybe something like\r\n\r\n> It therefore only superficially matches the GB18030-2005 standard for code points encoded as four bytes. It does not match the GB18030-2022 standard as that would increase the number of four-byte sequences mapping to Unicode Private Use Areas. The other direction for the impacted code points is handled by a side table in the gb18030 encoder.",
